About us

Southern Cross Travel Insurance (SCTI) is a proud member of the Southern Cross whānau, shining brightly in the market in both New Zealand and Australia. We’re incredibly proud to be the market leader and it’s an exciting time to join the beating heart of the business and to be there when our customers need us the most.



The needs and expectations of our customers are changing faster than ever, and we are right here with them providing assurance on their travels. We have a diverse and inclusive culture where team members are empowered to make decisions and succeed. Together, we are committed to achieving extraordinary results.



About the role:

Our Business Analyst plays a critical role in delivering successful projects by applying strong business analysis expertise across a diverse portfolio of initiatives. These can be varied but may include product development, new distribution partnerships, regulatory projects or process improvement.



This role involves eliciting, analysing, and documenting requirements, facilitating collaboration across a range of stakeholders (internal & external), and ensuring that project solutions meet business objectives, from efficiency initiatives to enabling growth.



As part of the PMO team, the Business Analyst also supports governance and delivery frameworks, ensuring consistency in working practices and alignment with organisational strategy.



About you:

5 years of business analysis experience across diverse projects
Strong ability to elicit, document, and validate business, functional, and technical requirements
Skilled in analysing and optimising business processes
Experience working within PMO governance frameworks
Expertise in collaborating with cross-functional teams to drive outcomes
Familiar with Agile, Waterfall, and hybrid project management methodologies
Proficient in creating project documentation, dashboards, and portfolio reports
Knowledge of risk and issue management, including mitigation strategies
Hands-on experience with business analysis tools (JIRA, Confluence, Visio)
Financial Services/Insurance industry experience would be advantageous


